{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Cittaka","html":"<article id='thag1.22'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.22 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.22 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cittakattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cittaka </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Nīlā sugīvā sikhino, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Crested peacocks with beautiful blue necks </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Morā kārambhiyaṁ abhinadanti; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>cry out in Karaṁvī. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Te sītavātakīḷitā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stirred by a cool breeze, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suttaṁ jhāyaṁ nibodhentī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they wake the sleeper to practice absorption. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Cittako thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
